  "answer": "A standalone Command Palette has been requested before. PowerToys#42103 and #38684 ask for a version you can install without the rest of PowerToys. In #38684 the maintainers said they will probably do this in the future. #44901 tracks running CmdPal unpackaged, which covers your use case of people who can't sideload or install apps. In that ticket, extracting the CmdPal .msix as a zip and running Microsoft.CmdPal.UI.exe works, and a portable mode is under discussion. Please add your zip workaround and your non-admin scenario as a comment on #44901 or #42103 instead of opening a new request. Also note that the .msix-to-zip route had quirks, such as settings and state files being written to %localappdata%\\Microsoft.CmdPal, and the app being reinstalled from the Store. The reinstall problem was fixed in later versions. Be careful about running zips from third-party repos, because users have to trust the build."
 },
